{"id":"lbe-restricted-affiliates-paid","title":"Recorded affiliates of certified firms that the City pays","question":"Which certified local firms have a recorded affiliate that is itself a City payee or prime contractor, and how much larger is it?","finding":"166 directory firms name 229 restricted affiliates; 62 affiliate names are City payees or prime contractors by name. In 19 the affiliate is not itself certified and was paid at least $5.0 million and 5 times what the certified firm was paid since fiscal 2019; the largest: Architectural Material Solutions, Inc. beside CLARK CONSTRUCTION GROUP - CALIF LP ($708.6 million).","how":"Each restricted affiliate name is matched to the payment file (fiscal 2019 on) and to prime-contractor and joint-venture rows in the contract file. \"Larger\" uses the rule in the “aliases” analysis: paid at least $5.0 million and at least 5 times the certified firm.","limits":"The City recorded these affiliations itself, so nothing here is hidden from it; the question is whether credit was given where the affiliate did the work, which needs the subcontractor payment reports. Size limits for certification are not in any file on disk; a large affiliate does not by itself make a firm ineligible. Name matches can be wrong for common names.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"lbe","t":"Certified firm","type":"org"},{"k":"cert","t":"Certification type","type":"text"},{"k":"size","t":"Size category as printed","type":"text"},{"k":"lbePaid","t":"City paid it since FY2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"lbeTeams","t":"Contract teams it is on","type":"int"},{"k":"affiliate","t":"Restricted affiliate","type":"org"},{"k":"affPaid","t":"City paid the affiliate","type":"usd"},{"k":"affPrime","t":"Affiliate's prime and joint-venture amounts in the contract file","type":"usd"},{"k":"affCertified","t":"Affiliate also certified","type":"text"},{"k":"big","t":"Larger by the rule","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"lbe":"Architectural Material Solutions, Inc.","lbeKey":"","si